  "details": "Using latest play store version of android vrchat application\n\nDevice: Samsung S24 Ultra\n\nNetwork: Stable Wi-Fi (with and without VPN)\n\nBattery mode: Not using any battery saving features, even explicitly disabled all battery optimisation features for the app.\n\nOptions: I'm hoping none of the mic related features are tied to FPS but I've locked it down to 30FPS. Will also \n\nReproduce:\n\nAfter being in a world for 5-15 minutes microphone stops working properly. \n\nParts of audio is being cut off. Later, after 15-20 minutes the microphone stops working entirely.\n\nThis is not a one time issue.. it's happening to me constantly :(\n\nI checked mic sensitivity, it is all the way to minimum to allow constant speech transfer. There's no noise suppression toggle on android version, so it's not that. \n\nI've tried: \n\n1. Reinstalling the app\n\n2. Turning ON and Turning OFF VPN\n\n3. Tried using cellular and stable Wi-Fi\n\n4. Samsung has mode for \"gaming\" modes. I've tried Performance, Balanced and Battery optimisation modes, all of which lead to the same scenario..\n\nI just wanna talk to frens :(",
